    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181-a3">

                <pb facs="0302" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg222"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ragsdale to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tientsin,
                                China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-02-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 224.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm your telegram
                    of this date with reference to the arrest of Krippendorf by the German consul.
                    It is unnecessary for me to say that I felt that intervention should not be
                    made, but the German consul had serious doubts about the matter and desired me
                    to place the matter before you before transporting the prisoner.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James W. Ragsdale</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
